expected_issues.description:
This block unconditionally overwrites `$columnData['sortable']` with an empty array. If earlier logic (or user config) already set `sortable` (e.g., `true`, `false`, or options), this will wipe it out. Consider only setting it when not already defined, or merging with existing config to avoid unexpected behavior.

```suggestion
                if (in_array($type['name'], [
                    'time',
                ])) {
                    $columnData['time'] = [];

                    // Preserve existing sortable configuration if already set.
                    $columnData['sortable'] ??= [];
                }
```

